4382 #edb/ref 1069 "q-84989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354382 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354382 #edb/ref 1071 "The $12$ members of a student council are asked to elect among themselves a leadership team: a president, a vice-president, and a secretary. How many different leadership teams are possible?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354382 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99b2f516-70c2-5e55-a428-0efe2c5f0628" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354382 #edb/ref 1074 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $12$ members to choose from, so $n=12.$ We want to select $3$ of those members to be in the leadership team, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different $3$-member leadership teams is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{12}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{12!}{(12-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{9!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10\\cdot \\cancel{9!}}{\\cancel{9!}} \\\\  & =12\\cdot 11\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =1\\,320.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354561 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186353905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354561 #edb/ref 1069 "q-87262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354561 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354561 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "98c1f989-8fe6-518d-bf14-b7c905f21857" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354561 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.5+P(B)-0.4 \\\\ P(B) & =0.8+0.4-0.5 \\\\ P(B) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363420 #edb/ref 1759218604541