ref 1069 "q-162649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363451 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363451 #edb/ref 1071 "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)^{2}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363451 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90dab51f-a29c-5cbc-905e-4caff26f179f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363451 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $(t+1)^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n2t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186363453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363452 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "058071f4-384f